{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-139184",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $x$-axis by solving the following equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}-{x}^{4} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{4}-2{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}(2-x) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $x=0$ and $x=2.$ So, we need to integrate from $x=0$ to $x=2.$ \n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}x(2{x}^{3}-{x}^{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(2{x}^{4}-{x}^{5})\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
